Lucciola: the login form looks like the lock screen's

The field's outline while it has the focus uses the secondary colour instead of
the primary, which greeter.toml keeps in the background's colour so that only
text shows (it also rings the account picture and fills the selected menu row).
Noctalia's lock screen draws its field the same way: sand around the field,
twice the width of the resting border.

The field alone is centred, like the picture and the name above it, with the
arrow outside it, and the status line is centred under the form: the arrow no
longer pushes the field to the left of everything else.

37 more pixels between the name and the field, the room the lock screen needs
there for its messages, so the two forms have one shape.

Applied by lucciola/greeter/noctalia-greeter.spec to the v1.7.0 tag, after 0006.
A look of Lucciola's, not proposed upstream.

diff --git a/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp b/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp
